Riaz Counseling also lists Depression & Anxiety among its specializations and identifies approaches including Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) and Dialectical Behavior Therapy (DBT).

### What to Expect When Starting Therapy

If you have never attended therapy, it is normal to feel uncertain about what to expect.

The process generally begins with a conversation about what has brought you to counseling.

Your therapist may ask about:

- What you have been experiencing
- When your symptoms began
- Whether you have noticed seasonal patterns
- How your mood affects everyday life
- Your personal goals for therapy
- Any previous experiences with mental health treatment

You can ask questions about the therapist's experience, approach, and whether their services are appropriate for your needs.

You do not need to arrive with a diagnosis or a complete explanation of what is happening. You can begin by describing what you have noticed.

